    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1">

                <pb facs="0011" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg1"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R.N.C./160: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Burdett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-01-13T23:00:00-03:00">January 13, 1941—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. For the Under Secretary<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1-f1"/> from Fenwick.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d1-f2"/> There will be no substantial difference between the
                    draft of the Security Zone Convention submitted to you as of December 14,<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d1-f3"/> and the final text to be agreed upon. Presumably, it
                    was not objectionable. As in the case of the Committee’s earlier recommendation,
                    the denial of port facilities would constitute the sole sanctions envisaged.
                    [Fenwick.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Burdett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
